{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And he said: Are you this one, etc.</b> That is, he vindicates his words that he is Esav — he is not asking. And Jacob's answer is in plain language: ״אָנִי״." "<b>Further,</b> it intends by his saying <b>you — this one</b>, that since his voice indicated that he was Jacob, therefore he aimed to bless the body that is physically before him, deciding that he is Esav. And therefore he said ״you — this one,״ pointing with his finger to that which the sense of touch reveals, and he would clothe the blessings in his mind with what was before him without any thought of who it was. And this is a good sign that Jacob received the blessings directed toward him, for even though Yitzchak finished speaking and mentioned Esav, with all that, at the time of the blessing he was blessing none other than this one before him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:50.200581927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}